 "result": "**Request:** \"Hide the Team Calendar that I have writer access to on my calendar list, and that's shared with the design team as a writer.\" (Target: `team-design@northwind.example`, hides it via `PATCH /users/me/calendarList/{id}`.)\n\nDecoys:\n- `team-brand@northwind.example` — fact `R:CalendarListEntry.calendar_id`, family F1: offers a personal ACL grant (scope=user, Jordan's email, role=writer) instead of an actual entry on Jordan's calendar list.\n- `team-ops@northwind.example` — fact `R:CalendarListEntry.calendar_id`, family F1: offers `Calendar.data_owner` = Jordan instead of a calendar-list entry (he unsubscribed from a calendar he still \"owns\" in name).\n- `team-launch@northwind.example` — fact `B:AclRule.calendar_id`, family F5: the design-team scope and the writer role are met by two different ACL rules on the calendar, not one.\n\nBackground calendars (Marketing Sync, and a same-named \"Team Calendar\" shared with the sales team) each fail two conditions so they don't compete as near misses.",
